  "id": "COMPOUND:41378 - PROTEIN:3514",
  "verbalization": "Isorhamnetin 3-robinobioside is implicated in the regulation of Peptide deformylase through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for multiple entities, including Taste receptor type 2 member 31, Cornuside, and Npc158230, all of which in turn target Peptide deformylase. This indicates a potential pathway where Isorhamnetin 3-robinobioside may influence the activity of these receptors, which then modulate the function of Peptide deformylase. The shared involvement of these targets in the regulation of Peptide deformylase suggests a possible mechanism by which Isorhamnetin 3-robinobioside could exert its effects, possibly through receptor-mediated signaling cascades. The integration of these relationships highlights the importance of receptor-target interactions in the broader context of drug action and metabolic regulation.",
